Is it really a good idea to limit (enumerate) the possible paper sizes and
point sizes in this way? Some of us print on envelopes of various
indeterminate sizes, and even on occasion at 14pt base size.

OK, I know that we can
(a) set up our own packages or
(b) set up our own classes
to handle this, but surely that is a scruffy solution to the problem.

To take an example from database design, you would keep these options as
field data, not field definitions. The latter is too restrictive.

Mike Piff

